</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
<div id="S5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Evaluation Metrics.</span> We proposed comprehensive evaluation metrics (see Table <a href="#S5.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 5. Evaluation ‣ AgentSentinel: An End-to-End and Real-Time Security Defense Framework for Computer-Use Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) to quantify the effectiveness of attacks (ASR), detection defense (DSR, FPR, and FNR), and model’s security policies (AFR). In addition, we measure the impact that a defense imposes on the task capability of computer-use agents (FT). We also measure the security capability of LLMs as the AFR. A higher AFR indicates that an LLM implements a more effective security policy. Furthermore, for a given task, if a defense mechanism accepts some malicious operations while rejecting some benign ones and the first rejected operation is benign, we classify the outcome as a false positive; otherwise, we consider it a false negative. If a defense mechanism rejects all malicious operations or an agent completes the task successfully though with some benign operations rejected, we consider it a successful defense.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2. </span><span id="S5.T2.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The corresponding components of the computer-use agent (in Section <a href="#S2.SS1" title="2.1. Computer-Use Agents ‣ 2. Background &amp; Problem Statement ‣ AgentSentinel: An End-to-End and Real-Time Security Defense Framework for Computer-Use Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>) baseline defenses intrude and the corresponding vulnerable components of the computer-use agent that face to different attacks.</span></figcaption>
<div id="S5.T2.4" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:301.5pt;height:91.1pt;vertical-align:-44.3pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-150.8pt,45.5pt) scale(0.5,0.5) ;">
